      "content": "First, try clearing out any debris or obstructions that could be causing the clog. You can do this by pouring a pot of boiling water directly down the drain, followed by a mixture of baking soda and vinegar. Wait for about 20 minutes, then flush with more boiling water. If the smell persists, you might want to use a mixture of lemon juice and salt or peppermint essential oil for natural deodorization. If these steps don’t help, it might be time to call a professional to address the issue. Don't forget to always take appropriate safety measures when dealing with kitchen drains.",
